><h2 class=3D"font-heading text-xl font-semibold mb-4">About</h2><p class=
=3D"text-foreground whitespace-pre-wrap leading-relaxed break-words">Worksp=
ace is a temporary place to share files and chat with people at a hackathon=
, workshop or meetup. The host creates a workspace and gets a QR code and a=
 6-digit PIN. Anyone can join by scanning or typing the PIN with just a nic=
kname, so there's no account, email or phone number to share.

you can access the website here: https://workspace-ystq.onrender.com

Inside, files open in a large viewer and chat sits beside them. You can pas=
te screenshots, @mention a file in a message, and search everything by mean=
ing: "wifi pw" finds "the network password is=E2=80=A6". Anyone who joins l=
ate sees the full history. When the host closes the workspace, or after at =
most 48 hours, everything is deleted automatically.

MongoDB makes the deletion work. Every message, file and member carries one=
 expiresAt date, and TTL indexes delete each document on time, so the app h=
as zero lines of delete code. Change streams push every new message and fil=
e to every phone instantly. Atlas Vector Search and Atlas Search are combin=
ed with $rankFusion for search by meaning, and Atlas creates the embeddings=
 itself, so they're deleted along with the documents. Unique indexes and sc=
hema validation stop duplicate PINs and oversized files.

The result is one database doing the job of five services: no separate file=
 storage, search engine, vector database, messaging service or cleanup jobs=
. It runs for $0 on an Atlas free cluster.

Built with: MongoDB Atlas, Next.js, Socket.IO, Render.</p></div></article><=
